=== let wages = dataset(wages)
let m = wages.reg(log(wage) ~ educ + exper + exper^2 + female + industry, se: robust)
let a = m.margins([educ, exper, female])
a.ci(exper, level: 0.9) ===
--- messages ---
error[Z0401]: `ci` of a test's result gives the intervals the test was made at, 95%, not at 90%
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:20
  |
4 | a.ci(exper, level: 0.9)
  |                    ^^^ another level
  |
  = help: run the test with `level:` for intervals at another level
[exit 1]

=== let wages = dataset(wages)
let m = wages.reg(log(wage) ~ educ + exper + exper^2 + female + industry, se: robust)
let a = m.margins([educ, exper, female])
report([a, m.test(educ == 0)]) ===
--- messages ---
error[Z0401]: `report` sets regressions side by side, but the second fit is a TestResult
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:8
  |
4 | report([a, m.test(educ == 0)])
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not a regression fit
  |
  = help: a test's result has no coefficients; report the fits it was made from
[exit 1]

=== let wages = dataset(wages)
let m = wages.reg(log(wage) ~ educ + exper + exper^2 + female + industry, se: robust)
let a = m.margins([educ, exper, female])
a.coef(exper) ===
--- messages ---
error[Z0414]: `exper` names a row, but `coef` reads no row of a test's result
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:8
  |
4 | a.coef(exper)
  |        ^^^^^ no row is taken here
  |
  = help: `p_values`, `std_errors`, `ci`, `statistic`, `df` and `effect_size` read one row by its name; `estimates()` gives every row of the table as a frame
[exit 1]
